# discovr build gate

Before writing or changing product code, UI, copy, structure, or APIs: **Read** the matching skills under `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (and their `reference.md` when the task is non-trivial). Skim `context/CURRENT.md` when present. Do not invent brand, voice, layout, or API rules.

| Work | Read first |
| --- | --- |
| Product / UX / pricing / inventory choice | `discovr-principles` |
| Any screen or component | `discovr-interface` + `discovr-brand` |
| Any user-facing string | `discovr-voice` |
| New file or folder | `discovr-structure` |
| Logo, favicon, splash, manifest icons | `discovr-logo` |
| PWA, launch, a11y, perf | `discovr-ship` |
| React / TypeScript implementation | `discovr-code` |
| Backend / `discovr-backend/` / Supabase / APIs / auth / SMS | `discovr-backend` |
| `@supabase/server` / auth modes / admin client | `supabase-server` |
| Updating skills or living system notes | `discovr-context` |

## After durable work

If you changed APIs, modules, env names, skills, or lasting product decisions: update `discovr-context-library` (or mirrored `.cursor/` + `context/CURRENT.md`) in the same session and push — see skill `discovr-context`.

## Always true

- Tokens only — raw hex in components is a bug.
- One `brand-primary` fill per screen.
- Full wordmark only — never a monogram.
- Every listing carries a one-line verdict.
- Dark-only — no light theme machinery.
- Folder shape: `features|shared/<name>/{components,utils,styles}`.
- Backend: one API process; HTTP → module facades only (`catalog`, `communication`, `user`, `auth`).
- Frontend owns UI/UX: layout, sections, order, how things look, and UI logic. Backend owns data, user-level logic and auth. No layout or display hints in tables or API responses.
